%N A397122 Prime reached by iterating A401006 starting at n, or -1 if no prime is reached.
%H A397122 Michael S. Branicky, <a href="/A397122/b397122.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..3686</a> (terms 1..307 from Derek Steinkamp)
%H A397122 Derek Steinkamp, <a href="/A397122/a397122.txt">Python Program</a>.
%F A397122 a(p) = p for p prime.
%F A397122 a(1) = -1.
%F A397122 a(A401006(n)) = a(n) for n >= 1.
%e A397122 a(1) = -1 since every iterate of 1 is 1, which is not prime.
%e A397122 a(4) = 211 since 4 -> 22 -> 211, prime.
%e A397122 a(8) = 67 since 8 -> 42 -> 67, prime.
%e A397122 a(49) = 131321 since 49 -> 77 -> 711 -> 979 -> 1189 -> 2941 -> 17173 -> 131321, prime.
